name: resources
description: >-
  Centralize shared JRebirth UI resources (images, fonts, styles, labels, sizes,
  colors) through resource enums and items. Use when adding assets or replacing
  magic constants and raw getResource strings.
---
# Create Resources

Centralize shared UI resources and avoid magic constants.

## Typical content

- label and text keys
- image and icon references
- CSS references
- spacing, sizes, and colors

## Key API

- images: an enum implementing `ImageEnum`, each entry calling `rel("basename", ImageExtension.PNG)`; read with `.get()`.
- styles: a `StyleSheetItem` from `Resources.create(new StyleSheet("Main"))`.
- prefer typed resource enums over raw `getResource("/path")` strings, so JPMS module access stays correct.

Template: `templates/ResourcesTemplate.java.txt`.
